     1,
     "Dear list,<p>How can we do cdf plot using ggplot2?<p>Thanks.<br></p></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "OFAvM4ikNhAJ",
   "from": "Ben Bond-Lamberty",
   "author": "f4249b01b99d0091",
   "date": "2012-04-20T10:22:27Z",
   "subject": "Re: CDF plot in ggplot2",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On Thu, Apr 19, 2012 at 8:53 AM, Jinyan Huang &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jhuan...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; How can we do cdf plot using ggplot2?"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<p>q &lt;- seq(-5,5,.1)<br>qplot(q,pnorm(q))<p>?<p>Ben<br></p></p></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "uqpAW24sRykJ",
   "from": "John Rauser",
   "author": "a523f4070ecfcf39",
   "date": "2012-04-23T04:03:46Z",
   "subject": "Re: CDF plot in ggplot2",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\">Or perhaps you&#39;re interested in the empirical CDF.  The trick is to use the line geom, which sorts the points in increasing x-axis order:</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">\n<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">x&lt;-rnorm(100)</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">qplot(x,ecdf(x)(x),geom=&quot;line&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>Does that help?</div><div><br></div><div>-J</div><div><br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">\nOn Fri, Apr 20, 2012 at 3:22 AM, Ben Bond-Lamberty <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bpb...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\n<div>On Thu, Apr 19, 2012 at 8:53 AM, Jinyan Huang &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jhuan...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>\n&gt; How can we do cdf plot using ggplot2?<br>\n<br>\n</div>q &lt;- seq(-5,5,.1)<br>\nqplot(q,pnorm(q))<br>\n<br>\n?<br>\n<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br>\nBen<br>\n</font></span></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
