  {
   "id": "ULDKdHg1BLoJ",
   "from": "David Kahle",
   "author": "e4aec126ff1dca22",
   "date": "2012-04-23T04:42:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: CDF plot in ggplot2",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Slight correction, the &#39;step&#39; geom is warranted -<div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 14px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(5,36,153)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">x </span>&lt;-<span style=\"color:#065218\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:#065218\">10</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 14px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(5,36,153)\">qplot(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>,ecdf(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>)(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>), <span style=\"color:#000000\">geom </span>= <span style=\"color:#b0140f\">&quot;line&quot;</span>)</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 14px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(5,36,153);min-height:19px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 14px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(5,36,153)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">r </span>&lt;- extendrange(range(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>))</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 14px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(5,36,153)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">s</span> &lt;- seq(<span style=\"color:#000000\">r</span>[<span style=\"color:#065218\">1</span>], <span style=\"color:#000000\">r</span>[<span style=\"color:#065218\">2</span>], <span style=\"color:#000000\">length.out </span>= <span style=\"color:#065218\">501</span>)</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 14px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(5,36,153)\">qplot(<span style=\"color:#000000\">s</span>, ecdf(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>)(<span style=\"color:#000000\">s</span>), <span style=\"color:#000000\">geom </span>= <span style=\"color:#b0140f\">&quot;step&quot;</span>)</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 14px/normal Monaco;color:rgb(5,36,153)\">plot(ecdf(<span style=\"color:#000000\">x</span>))</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>david.</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><br></div><div><div>On Apr 22, 2012, at 11:03 PM, John Rauser wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\">Or perhaps you&#39;re interested in the empirical CDF.  The trick is to use the line geom, which sorts the points in increasing x-axis order:</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">\r\n<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">x&lt;-rnorm(100)</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">qplot(x,ecdf(x)(x),geom=&quot;line&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div>Does that help?</div><div><br></div><div>-J</div><div><br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">\r\nOn Fri, Apr 20, 2012 at 3:22 AM, Ben Bond-Lamberty <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bpb...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div>On Thu, Apr 19, 2012 at 8:53 AM, Jinyan Huang &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jhuan...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>\r\n&gt; How can we do cdf plot using ggplot2?<br>\r\n<br>\r\n</div>q &lt;- seq(-5,5,.1)<br>\r\nqplot(q,pnorm(q))<br>\r\n<br>\r\n?<br>\r\n<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br>\r\nBen<br>\r\n</font></span><div><div><br>\r\n--<br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376089878000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2r9k0JSiM234F9MPD1KEbY\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n<br>\r\nTo post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href